\chapter{Guided mode, stage three}

Stage three teaches one knot step by step. The overhand knot is the first guided
lesson. The page shows its steps in order, and a step is done only when the
recogniser confirms it. A timer never advances a step, and a click never does.

\section{What a step is}

Each lesson step has the instruction the player reads, and a check. A check is a
fact about the rope that the recogniser computes from a snapshot. The check is one
of two kinds. A crossings check passes when the diagram has at least a given
number of crossings. A knot check passes when the recogniser names the knot. The
lesson is finished when every step passes.

@d Lessons: guided steps @{
// A check is a fact about the rope that the recogniser computes.
export type StepCheck = { kind: 'crossings'; atLeast: number } | { kind: 'knot'; name: string };

export interface LessonStep {
  text: string;
  check: StepCheck;
}
@}

\section{The check for a step}

The first step whose check fails is the current step. Steps are not remembered
once passed. If the player undoes a crossing, the lesson goes back to the step
that needs it. That is why the crossing checks are cumulative: a rope with three
crossings passes the first two.

A crossing count depends on how the rope is turned, because the diagram is read
along the depth axis. The page does not correct for it. A player who turns the rope
may see a crossing count change without changing the knot.

@d Guided: step check @{
import type { KnotResult } from '../topology/recogniser';
import type { LessonStep, StepCheck } from './record';

export function checkPasses(check: StepCheck, result: KnotResult | null): boolean {
  if (!result) return false;
  if (check.kind === 'crossings') return result.crossings >= check.atLeast;
  return result.name === check.name;
}

// The index of the current step: the first whose check fails. Equal to steps.length when all pass.
export function currentStep(steps: readonly LessonStep[], result: KnotResult | null): number {
  const index = steps.findIndex((step) => !checkPasses(step.check, result));
  return index === -1 ? steps.length : index;
}
@}

\section{The panel}

The panel lists the steps. Steps before the current one are marked done, the
current one is highlighted, and the rest are muted. When every step passes the
panel says the lesson is complete. The panel receives the recogniser's result from
the page, and the page updates it only when the name or the crossings change.

@d UI: guided panel @{
import type { LessonStep } from '../lessons/record';
import { currentStep } from '../lessons/guided';
import type { KnotResult } from '../topology/recogniser';

export function GuidedPanel({ steps, result }: { steps: readonly LessonStep[]; result: KnotResult | null }) {
  const current = currentStep(steps, result);
  return (
    <div className="mt-2">
      <ol className="list-decimal space-y-0.5 pl-5 text-sm">
        {steps.map((step, index) => {
          const tone =
            index < current ? 'text-emerald-400' : index === current ? 'font-semibold text-slate-100' : 'text-slate-500';
          return (
            <li key={step.text} className={tone}>
              {index < current ? '✓ ' : ''}
              {step.text}
            </li>
          );
        })}
      </ol>
      <p className="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-300">
        {current === steps.length ? 'Lesson complete.' : `Step ${current + 1} of ${steps.length}.`}
      </p>
    </div>
  );
}
@}

\section{Tests}

The tests drive the lesson with the recogniser's own results. A straight rope has
no crossings, so no step passes. The scripted trefoil passes every step. A rope
that loses a crossing goes back to the step that needs it.

@d Guided: tests @{
import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';
import type { Vec3 } from '../rope/snapshot';
import { recognise } from '../topology/recogniser';
import { STAGE_ONE_LESSONS } from './record';
import { currentStep } from './guided';

const steps = STAGE_ONE_LESSONS[0].steps;

const trefoil = (t: number): Vec3 => ({
  x: Math.sin(t) + 2 * Math.sin(2 * t),
  y: Math.cos(t) - 2 * Math.cos(2 * t),
  z: -Math.sin(3 * t),
});

const sample = (curve: (t: number) => Vec3, n: number): Vec3[] =>
  Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => curve((2 * Math.PI * i) / n));

describe('guided overhand lesson', () => {
  it('starts at the first step with no result', () => {
    expect(currentStep(steps, null)).toBe(0);
  });

  it('does not advance for a straight rope', () => {
    const straight = Array.from({ length: 40 }, (_, i) => ({ x: i * 0.05, y: 0, z: 0 }));
    expect(currentStep(steps, recognise({ points: straight, radius: 0.02 }))).toBe(0);
  });

  it('is complete for the scripted trefoil', () => {
    const tied = recognise({ points: sample(trefoil, 120), radius: 0.02 });
    expect(currentStep(steps, tied)).toBe(steps.length);
  });

  it('goes back to the step that needs a crossing that is undone', () => {
    const tied = recognise({ points: sample(trefoil, 120), radius: 0.02 });
    expect(currentStep(steps, tied)).toBe(steps.length);
    const undone = { ...tied, crossings: 1 };
    expect(currentStep(steps, undone)).toBe(1);
  });
});
@}
